From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dtc: recognise the thermal cooling-map trip phandle property

A cooling map's trip reaches its trip point by bare phandle. Without it in
the table the cell stays numeric, and a number that means a node is only
valid for the exact allocation it was dumped from.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/livetree.c b/livetree.c
--- a/livetree.c
+++ b/livetree.c
@@ -1191,6 +1191,7 @@ static const struct phandle_prop phandle_props[] = {
 	{ "io-channels",		"#io-channel-cells" },
 	{ "interrupt-parent",		NULL },
 	{ "cpu-idle-states",		NULL },
+	{ "trip",			NULL },
 	{ "interrupt-affinity",		NULL },
 	{ "devfreq-events",		NULL },
 	{ "extcon",			NULL },
